# Tooltips for how a control works

Member-facing pages explain a control with `SiteTooltip` (`src/components/SiteTooltip.tsx`). Hover or focus on the control shows `site-tooltip-panel`.

Do not leave a paragraph under a form that tells the member what the checkboxes, radios, or fields mean.

Do not use the browser `title` attribute for hover text. That is the plain system tooltip. `SiteTooltip` is the one members should see, including on links that would otherwise forward `title` to the anchor.

## Use a tooltip

- What a checkbox, radio, button, or field does
- A limit or requirement (ships under 4 SCU, sign-in, RSI verified)
- How a choice is made (closest shop, random among the best payers)

```tsx
<SiteTooltip side="top" content="Off, the run stays in the system you start in.">
  <label className="flex items-center gap-2">
    <input type="checkbox" className="site-checkbox" />
    Cross system
  </label>
</SiteTooltip>
```

## Keep text on the page

- A result of what they just did (no matches, the route changed, UEX could not be checked)
- An empty list
- The step they are on (where to go, what to buy, the aUEC figures)

One or two sentences in the tooltip. The Information Archive still holds the full how-to.
